---
import Footer from "@components/Footer.astro";
import Navbar from "@components/Navbar.astro";
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import "@styles/global.css";
import "@styles/tokens.css";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use — Nimbus"
  description="Terms and conditions for using the Nimbus WordPress plugin and website."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content" class="legal-page">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="back-link" href="/">
        <svg
          width="14"
          height="14"
          viewBox="0 0 16 16"
          fill="none"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path
            d="M10 3L5 8l5 5"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.6"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
        </svg>
        Back to Nimbus
      </a>

      <article class="legal-article">
        <header class="legal-header">
          <p class="section-label">Legal</p>
          <h1 class="legal-title">Terms of Use</h1>
          <p class="legal-date">Last updated: 28 July 2026</p>
        </header>

        <div class="legal-body">
          <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
          <p>
            By downloading or using the Nimbus WordPress plugin ("Software"),
            you agree to be bound by these Terms of Use ("Terms"). If you do
            not agree, you may not use the Software. These Terms govern your
            use of the Software and the Nimbus website (usenimbus.dev).
          </p>

          <h2>2. License grant</h2>
          <p>
            Nimbus is free and open-source software licensed under the
            <strong>GNU General Public License v2.0 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later)</strong>.
            You may install, use, modify, and redistribute the Software on any
            number of WordPress sites, free of charge, subject to the terms of
            the GPL. The full license text is available at
            <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-2.0.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >gnu.org/licenses/gpl-2.0.html</a
            >. There is no license key, no paid tier, and no restriction on the
            number of sites you may run the Software on.
          </p>

          <h2>3. Source code and contributions</h2>
          <p>
            The Software's source code is publicly available. Contributions,
            bug reports, and feature requests are welcome via the project's
            source repository. Contributions you submit are accepted under the
            same GPL-2.0-or-later license as the rest of the project unless
            otherwise agreed in writing.
          </p>

          <h2>4. Support</h2>
          <p>
            Nimbus is supported on a best-effort, community basis via the
            WordPress.org support forum, the project's issue tracker, and
            email at <a href="mailto:hello@usenimbus.dev">hello@usenimbus.dev</a>.
            There is no guaranteed response time or service-level agreement.
          </p>

          <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
          <p>
            The Software integrates with third-party cloud storage providers
            (Amazon S3, Cloudflare R2, etc.) and cache plugins that you
            configure yourself. Your use of those services is governed by
            their respective terms and privacy policies. Nimbus is not
            responsible for the actions, availability, or data handling
            practices of any third-party provider you choose to connect.
          </p>

          <h2>6. Trademarks</h2>
          <p>
            "Nimbus" and the Nimbus logo are used to identify this project.
            While the Software's code is licensed under the GPL, this does not
            grant permission to use the Nimbus name or logo to imply
            endorsement of a competing or forked product.
          </p>

          <h2>7. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
          <p>
            THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,
            EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF
            MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND
            NON-INFRINGEMENT. NIMBUS DOES NOT WARRANT THAT THE SOFTWARE WILL BE
            ERROR-FREE, UNINTERRUPTED, OR FREE OF SECURITY VULNERABILITIES.
          </p>

          <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p>
            TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, IN NO EVENT
            SHALL NIMBUS OR ITS CONTRIBUTORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT,
            INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, INCLUDING
            LOSS OF DATA, REVENUE, OR PROFITS, ARISING OUT OF OR RELATED TO
            YOUR USE OF THE SOFTWARE.
          </p>

          <h2>9. Governing law</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with
            applicable law. Any disputes arising under these Terms shall be
            resolved through good-faith negotiation first, and failing that,
            through the competent courts of the developer's jurisdiction.
          </p>

          <h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            We may update these Terms from time to time. When we do, we will
            update the "last updated" date above. Continued use of the
            Software after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the
            revised Terms.
          </p>

          <h2>11. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about these Terms? Email us at <a
              href="mailto:hello@usenimbus.dev">hello@usenimbus.dev</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding: 3.5rem 0 7rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--nmb-text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    transition: color var(--nmb-t);
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--nmb-text);
  }

  /* ── Article ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .legal-article {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--nmb-border-light);
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    color: var(--nmb-text);
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0.25rem;
  }

  .legal-date {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--nmb-text-subtle);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Body typography ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .legal-body h2 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--nmb-text);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.625rem;
  }

  .legal-body p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--nmb-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin: 0 0 0.875rem;
  }

  .legal-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 0.875rem 1.25rem;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .legal-body li {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--nmb-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .legal-body strong {
    color: var(--nmb-text-2);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .legal-body a {
    color: var(--nmb-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .legal-body a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
